INCLUDED IN THIS REPOSITORY

None. Everything here was written for this project, and there are no third-party
libraries, fonts or samples in it.


USED, NOT INCLUDED

ffmpeg
  Optional. When someone has installed it, the engine runs it as a separate program
  to read formats that macOS can't. It isn't bundled, and the tests use it to make
  tiny clips. https://ffmpeg.org

ExifTool by Phil Harvey
  Used in the tests, when it's installed, to check the engine's reading of Sony's rtmd
  data track. Its published tag tables were the reference for that track's layout.
  None of its code is in Select. https://exiftool.org

Oklab by Bjorn Ottosson
  The colour space the engine measures dominant colours in. The published matrices are
  used. https://bottosson.github.io/posts/oklab/

Sony S-Log3 and S-Gamut3.Cine
  The engine uses Sony's published curve and primaries to read log footage.

Apple Vision and SoundAnalysis
  The models that label pictures and sounds ship with macOS and run on the Mac.

Adobe ZXPSignCmd
  Used by the maintainer to sign the panel. It isn't bundled.
  https://github.com/Adobe-CEP/CEP-Resources

Adobe Common Extensibility Platform and Premiere Pro
  The panel runs inside them. Premiere Pro is a trademark of Adobe.

Apple VideoToolbox, AudioToolbox and other macOS frameworks
  The engine links against them as they ship with macOS.
